'''''Aristolochia baetica''''', the '''Andalusian Dutchman's pipe''' or '''pipe vine''', is a poisonous perennial vine that occurs in [[North Africa]] and the southern [[Iberian Peninsula]], from [[Algeria]] to [[Portugal]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Aristolochia baetica |url=http://www.floraiberica.es/floraiberica/texto/pdfs/01_033_01_Aristolochia.pdf |publisher=[[Flora Iberica]] |access-date=1 July 2021}}</ref><ref name="herbarium">{{cite web | url=http://www.herbarium.rdg.ac.uk/mediplants/resultd.asp?SP=Aristolochia%20baetica | title=Herbarium aristolochia baetica information | publisher=[[University of Reading]] | date=August 21, 2006 | accessdate=June 7, 2011| archiveurl= https://web.archive.org/web/20110721223059/http://www.herbarium.rdg.ac.uk/mediplants/resultd.asp?SP=Aristolochia%20baetica| archivedate= 21 July 2011 | url-status= live}}</ref><ref name="alora">{{cite web|url=http://www.aloraseeds.com/cgi-bin/product.asp?ProdID=33 |title=Alora seeds Aristolochia baetica product |publisher=Aloraseeds.com |date=16 Jun 2010 |accessdate=June 7, 2011 |url-status=dead |archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20110903195725/http://www.aloraseeds.com/cgi-bin/product.asp?ProdID=33 |archivedate=September 3, 2011 }}</ref>

==Description==
''Aristolochia baetica'' is a rarely procumbent [[evergreen]] climber with triangular, cordate, glaucous lobes a quarter the size of the leaves.<ref name="herbarium" /> Flowers vary from 2 to 5 centimetres and are from brownish-purple to reddish.<ref name="herbarium" />

